</p>

<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>What is Image SEO?</h3>

<p>
Image SEO is the process of optimizing images so search engines can understand,
index, and rank them effectively.
</p>

<h3>Does alt text improve SEO?</h3>

<p>
Yes. Alt text provides context for search engines and improves accessibility,
making it an important component of Image SEO.
</p>

<h3>What image format is best for SEO?</h3>

<p>
WebP is generally the best balance between compression, quality, and browser
support. AVIF may provide even smaller file sizes.
</p>

<h3>Do file names matter?</h3>

<p>
Yes. Descriptive file names help search engines understand image content and
provide additional relevance signals.
</p>

<h3>Do images affect website speed?</h3>

<p>
Absolutely. Images are often the largest assets on a webpage and can
significantly influence loading performance.
</p>

<h3>Should every image have alt text?</h3>

<p>
Most content images should have descriptive alt text. Decorative images may
use empty alt attributes when appropriate.
</p>

<h3>What is an image sitemap?</h3>

<p>
An image sitemap helps search engines discover and index images more
efficiently.
</p>

<h3>Does Image SEO help Google Images rankings?</h3>

<p>
Yes. Proper optimization improves the likelihood of appearing in Google Images
search results.
</p>

<h3>What is the relationship between Image SEO and Core Web Vitals?</h3>

<p>
Optimized images improve loading speed and can contribute directly to better
Core Web Vitals performance.
</p>

<h3>Can Image SEO increase traffic?</h3>

<p>
Yes. Many websites receive substantial traffic from image search platforms,
especially when images are optimized correctly.
</p>

